Template: hnlink/call
Type: string
Description: Callsign and SSID for hnlink:
 hnlink transmits under this AX.25 address. Use an SSID that nothing else on
 the TNC uses (Winlink, APRS), e.g. KN6FLN-5.
 .
 Leave it empty to set CALL in /etc/hnlink.conf later; hnlink does not run
 until it is set.

Template: hnlink/from
Type: string
Description: From: line for posts made on the hnlink status page:
 For example: KN6FLN <you@example.com>. Empty means the bare callsign.

Template: hnlink/call-invalid
Type: error
Description: "${call}" is not a callsign-SSID
 Use the form CALL or CALL-N with N from 0 to 15, e.g. KN6FLN-5.
